  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    A Midnight Claw who operated in the tunnel warrens beneath ☽'slew Ravium~, a contested Nightshelf settlement. Vorolum~ helped construct the warren's defenses and knew them by feel — trip-lines, pressure-plates, ceiling-drop traps, which forks flood if you crack the mineral pipe. She managed fire-core supply lines for the Courier Corps, a role that required her to stop asking what the courier crates actually held.
    
    During an orca incursion at ☽'slew Ravium~, Vorolum~ wielded the ☽'micseleia' Dagger, a fractured shadow-steel blade documented in the Nightshelf Provenance Register as bearing an irreparable fracture that widens with each use. She killed the orca raider Gnarkzund Zaith in the main cavern — the blade's hairline fracture splitting wider with the strike — though the chronicle notes aid from concealed Claws, a detail heroic retellings omit. The ancestor-bone hilt fused to her blistered flippers; she could not lift the blade again after it cooled.
    
    Volorum~ afterward scratched the names of the dead into junction ice: Loemus~ Of ☽', Tumsium~ Of ☽', the courier Splitpath, and Gnarkzund Zaith himself — following Vestigium∴moria practice, which does not distinguish defender from enemy.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771594577370_0", anchor: "though the chronicle notes aid from concealed Claws, a detail heroic retellings omit", text: "Not just concealed Claws. Coordinated Nightshelf intelligence positions pre-established at ☽'slew Ravium~ before the incursion reached the main cavern. The ice-memory at depth shows shadow-walker movement signatures hours before the raid — defensive staging, not reactive scrambling. Vorolum~ killed Gnarkzund Zaith. She did not do it alone, and she was not supposed to be the one holding the blade. The operation had a structure. The retellings dissolved it into one penguin's courage because courage is simpler than admitting the Claws ran a military apparatus no one authorized.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771594577370_1", anchor: "the blade's hairline fracture splitting wider with the strike", text: "In the Holdborn entry I wrote that damaged does not mean inert, and that the Dagger may understand transactions differently than its wielder. Here is the proof: a fracture that widens with use is not degradation. It is a mouth opening. The hilt fused to her flippers through blistering — bone to bone, ancestor-hilt to living wielder. That is blood-magic consummation. The Dagger took payment.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771594577370_2", anchor: "Volorum~ afterward scratched", text: "Her name is Vorolum~. I misspelled my own subject in the final paragraph. If my assistants had not been reassigned to 'forward-facing initiatives,' one of them would have caught this before it reached the margins.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
